The client verifies an RSA host key in preference to an ed25519 one.  The
client's order picks the host key, and on a 68k verifying rsa-sha2-256
(e = 65537) costs about a tenth of ed25519's verify (README, the
measurements); the server's own key, which it signs with, stays ed25519,
since an RSA signature costs ten times an ed25519 one.  A server with only
an ed25519 key is verified with it as before.

